docs {
  Sui gRPC API (`sui.rpc.v2`), served through Alchemy.

  **Endpoint:** `https://sui-mainnet.g.alchemy.com/`

  **Auth:** send your Alchemy API key as gRPC metadata:
  `X-Token: <api_key>` (set `api_key` in your Bruno environment).

  **Protos:** the real Sui v2 protos are vendored under `grpc/proto/sui/rpc/v2/`
  (source: https://github.com/MystenLabs/sui-apis/tree/main/proto/sui/rpc/v2).

  **Services covered, all live-verified against `sui-mainnet.g.alchemy.com`
  except where noted:**
  - `SubscriptionService` — `SubscribeCheckpoints`, the only streaming RPC
    Sui exposes (server-streaming). See `subscribe-checkpoints.bru`.
  - `LedgerService` (`ledger/`) — `GetServiceInfo`, `GetObject`,
    `BatchGetObjects`, `GetTransaction`, `BatchGetTransactions`,
    `GetCheckpoint`, `GetEpoch`.
  - `StateService` (`state/`) — `GetCoinInfo`, `GetBalance`, `ListBalances`,
    `ListOwnedObjects`, `ListDynamicFields`.
  - `MovePackageService` (`move-package/`) — `GetPackage`,
    `ListPackageVersions`, `GetDatatype`, `GetFunction`.
  - `SignatureVerificationService` (`signature-verification/`) —
    `VerifySignature`.
  - `TransactionExecutionService` (`transaction-execution/`) —
    `SimulateTransaction` (verified — doesn't mutate state) and
    `ExecuteTransaction` (**not** live-tested: it broadcasts a real signed
    transaction and moves funds, which needs a live private key — see that
    request's docs).

  All unary methods are unary; only `SubscribeCheckpoints` streams. Sui does
  not offer per-transaction, per-event, or per-object subscriptions.
}
